WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.667
-Why are you
the district attorney?

00:00:02.667 --> 00:00:06.234
Or are you just the illusion
of the district attorney?

00:00:06.234 --> 00:00:08.367
-'Cause I'm the hero
of that story.

00:00:08.367 --> 00:00:10.467
And as long as people
still believe in justice

00:00:10.467 --> 00:00:14.467
and there's a system in place
that looks like it works,

00:00:14.467 --> 00:00:18.467
I'm doing what the city
pays me to do.

00:00:18.467 --> 00:00:21.367
-[ Exhales sharply ]

00:00:21.367 --> 00:00:24.200
Who the [bleep]
wants to be any part of that?

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:25.634
-Welcome back to "Late Night."
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:25.634 --> 00:00:27.501
That was a clip
from "Perry Mason,"

00:00:27.501 --> 00:00:29.501
starring this guy, Matthew Rhys.

00:00:29.501 --> 00:00:32.934
Now, I do have
"Perry Mason" questions,

00:00:32.934 --> 00:00:34.133
but we mentioned your boat,
Rarebit.

00:00:34.133 --> 00:00:35.400
And this is -- you are --

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:37.300
Again, this speaks
to the kind of guest you are.

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:39.901
You have brought two foods.

00:00:39.901 --> 00:00:43.300
Because rarebit
I know to be a food, and I am --

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:44.901
But yet I don't know what it is.

00:00:44.901 --> 00:00:46.667
-Right. So, sorry.
I should have qualified.

00:00:46.667 --> 00:00:49.734
There is a traditional
Welsh dish called Welsh rarebit,

00:00:49.734 --> 00:00:52.901
which is basically
cheese on toast.

00:00:52.901 --> 00:00:55.667
Which speaks
to the kind of culinary,

00:00:55.667 --> 00:00:58.334
you know, prowess that I have.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:58.334 --> 00:00:59.801
That's about
the sum total of it.

00:00:59.801 --> 00:01:01.534
-And you make --
you do make this

00:01:01.534 --> 00:01:02.901
for your guests on your boat.

00:01:02.901 --> 00:01:04.734
-So I came up
with this ingenious idea

00:01:04.734 --> 00:01:07.267
that what I should do
when I'm aboard

00:01:07.267 --> 00:01:09.467
is prepare them
small Welsh rarebits,

00:01:09.467 --> 00:01:11.234
which is just
toasted bread, cheese.

00:01:11.234 --> 00:01:13.167
I have --
There is no oven or grill

00:01:13.167 --> 00:01:15.634
or broiler, anything,
so I use a blowtorch on --

00:01:15.634 --> 00:01:16.767
[ Laughter ]

00:01:16.767 --> 00:01:18.801
On a wooden boat.
-It's a wooden boat, yeah.

00:01:18.801 --> 00:01:20.200
I wanted to clarify that.
-Yeah.

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:21.767
[ Laughter ]

00:01:21.767 --> 00:01:24.601
-So they must be very excited
when they see an actor,

00:01:24.601 --> 00:01:27.334
not a sailor or a captain.
-No, no.

00:01:27.334 --> 00:01:29.901
Like, I tell people,
"Look, I've played a sailor.

00:01:29.901 --> 00:01:31.467
I've played a chef.
It's like...

00:01:31.467 --> 00:01:33.834
[ Light laughter ]
How badly can this go?

00:01:33.834 --> 00:01:36.100
I just think
it adds to the drama.

00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:37.534
I think it adds
to the drama of it all.

00:01:37.534 --> 00:01:39.767
-Give us a sense
of what they're seeing.

00:01:39.767 --> 00:01:42.601
-So what I do --
So, in fairness,

00:01:42.601 --> 00:01:44.300
your show, I don't think,
trusted me

00:01:44.300 --> 00:01:45.901
with the kind of blowtorch
that I use.

00:01:45.901 --> 00:01:48.200
-Okay.
-Mine's bigger, obviously.

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:50.067
[ Laughter ]

00:01:50.067 --> 00:01:52.434
So I --
I have to make it quickly.

00:01:52.434 --> 00:01:53.701
Therefore,
I use a large blowtorch.

00:01:53.701 --> 00:01:55.400
And I think
it adds to the drama.

00:01:55.400 --> 00:01:58.000
'Cause you see them going,
"Will we make it home alive?"

00:01:58.000 --> 00:01:59.100
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:00.567
-It's like, even I say,
"I don't know.

00:02:00.567 --> 00:02:01.834
Let's see how it goes.

00:02:01.834 --> 00:02:04.067
Do you like
cheese and toasted bread?"

00:02:04.067 --> 00:02:05.234
So all I --
-It is a funny thing

00:02:05.234 --> 00:02:06.567
to risk your life for.
-It is.

00:02:06.567 --> 00:02:08.734
But, basically,
this is the sped-up version

00:02:08.734 --> 00:02:10.033
we've done for you.
-Yeah.

00:02:10.033 --> 00:02:12.300
-So all I'm doing,
although this isn't --

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:14.501
The boat version -- right? --
'cause it's always rockin',

00:02:14.501 --> 00:02:16.467
so choppy, it's like that.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:16.467 --> 00:02:19.133
-Right. Yeah, yeah,
I wouldn't want to see that.

00:02:19.133 --> 00:02:20.267
-You're kind of doing that.

00:02:20.267 --> 00:02:21.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:21.634 --> 00:02:24.133
-And, also, it should be noted,
this is you making it

00:02:24.133 --> 00:02:27.100
on the boat,
and that's a real beard

00:02:27.100 --> 00:02:28.834
you had for a while there.
-It's a fake beard.

00:02:28.834 --> 00:02:30.567
I put on the wig
and the beard 'cause I'm like,

00:02:30.567 --> 00:02:32.000
"Arr!
Welcome to the boat!"

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:33.200
[ Laughter ]

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:34.734
And they're like,
"We can see the glue.

00:02:34.734 --> 00:02:36.234
It doesn't work."

00:02:36.234 --> 00:02:38.133
So, basically, that's all I do.

00:02:38.133 --> 00:02:40.534
And then I offer up
showbiz tales

00:02:40.534 --> 00:02:43.634
and all sorts and try
and wake them up for the end.

00:02:43.634 --> 00:02:44.934
-You said --
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.934 --> 00:02:47.067
You said the boat
is from the '30s.

00:02:47.067 --> 00:02:50.367
On "Perry Mason,"
you were on a '30s motorcycle.

00:02:50.367 --> 00:02:52.200
-I was.
-And this is practical.

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:54.767
You're riding this motorcycle.
-It is practical.

00:02:54.767 --> 00:02:57.434
However, on the first day,
they say, "Come do your trial --

00:02:57.434 --> 00:03:00.200
you know, your training
on the Harley-Davidson."

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:03.701
And then the guy who -- "Right,
this is how you start it.

00:03:03.701 --> 00:03:05.734
You turn this, you pull that,
you push this.

00:03:05.734 --> 00:03:06.934
Wait for that to kick in.

00:03:06.934 --> 00:03:09.534
Now push that, pull that again,
and you're off."

00:03:09.534 --> 00:03:11.100
And I was like...
[ Laughter ]

00:03:11.100 --> 00:03:13.133
And the producer
saw the wild-eyed panic

00:03:13.133 --> 00:03:14.601
in my eyes and went, "Okay.

00:03:14.601 --> 00:03:18.234
We need a montage to do just
the starting of the motorbike."

00:03:18.234 --> 00:03:19.701
Told the action guy vehicle,

00:03:19.701 --> 00:03:22.834
"Turn it into
an electric bike in a week."

00:03:22.834 --> 00:03:24.968
-Yeah.
-So it kind of split --

00:03:24.968 --> 00:03:27.734
A number of people who,
when we were shooting outside,

00:03:27.734 --> 00:03:28.968
would come out and say,
"Oh, my God.

00:03:28.968 --> 00:03:31.501
Is this a 1933 Harley?"
They're like, "It is."

00:03:31.501 --> 00:03:32.801
They're like,
"Why can't we hear it?"

00:03:32.801 --> 00:03:35.100
And I'd say, [weakly]
"It's an electric bike now."

00:03:35.100 --> 00:03:36.400
[ Laughter ]

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:39.167
And it would split.
50% of these predominantly men

00:03:39.167 --> 00:03:40.667
of a certain age would go,
"That's incredible.

00:03:40.667 --> 00:03:41.934
You've turned it
into an electric bike,"

00:03:41.934 --> 00:03:43.934
and 50% would say,
"That's disgusting,

00:03:43.934 --> 00:03:45.434
what you've done to that hog."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:45.434 --> 00:03:46.901
-I would say, like, yeah.
-I get it.

00:03:46.901 --> 00:03:49.133
-This, though, there's
no shortcut with horses.

00:03:49.133 --> 00:03:51.767
-There was no shortcuts.
-Now, this is you on a horse.

00:03:51.767 --> 00:03:54.000
-That's me on a horse.
-That's you on a horse.

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:57.901
-There's no CGI.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:57.901 --> 00:04:01.434
-Can I ask why --
-No saddle in that picture.

00:04:01.434 --> 00:04:02.634
-Look at that!
No saddle.

00:04:02.634 --> 00:04:03.901
-Yeah, yeah.
-It's interesting

00:04:03.901 --> 00:04:05.167
'cause saddles --
you would think you'd need

00:04:05.167 --> 00:04:06.501
a saddle for safety.

00:04:06.501 --> 00:04:09.200
You're doing no saddle,
but you are wearing a mask.

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:11.601
[ Laughter ]

00:04:11.601 --> 00:04:13.801
-The horse was an anti-vaxxer.

00:04:13.801 --> 00:04:15.767
-Oh.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:15.767 --> 00:04:17.033
Or had COVID.

00:04:17.033 --> 00:04:18.334
I couldn't understand
what he was trying to say.

00:04:18.334 --> 00:04:20.400
-Right, right, right.
It's very hard.

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:22.067
It's hard.
-It's hard.

00:04:22.067 --> 00:04:24.067
It's hard for them.
-Now, did you have any

00:04:24.067 --> 00:04:26.434
previous experience on a horse,
because this looks terrifying.

00:04:26.434 --> 00:04:29.968
-I actually did, and I did that
slightly foolish thing.

00:04:29.968 --> 00:04:31.400
The writers very kindly said,

00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:32.968
"Is there anything
you want to do in a scene?"

00:04:32.968 --> 00:04:34.834
And I was like,
"I love riding horses."

00:04:34.834 --> 00:04:36.801
But they put me on a scene
where the horse rears.

00:04:36.801 --> 00:04:39.000
I was like,
"I don't like horses that rear."

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:40.901
I like riding -- riding them.
-Yeah.

00:04:40.901 --> 00:04:42.934
-But it was a --
I loved it.

00:04:42.934 --> 00:04:44.567
I bonded with the horse.
-Well, there you go.

00:04:44.567 --> 00:04:46.434
And you guys will probably
work together again.

00:04:46.434 --> 00:04:49.200
-I hope so.
-Now, you've talked in the past,

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:50.601
again, one of
my all-time favorite shows

00:04:50.601 --> 00:04:52.167
where you met your partner,
Keri.

00:04:52.167 --> 00:04:54.200
-Yeah.
-And by the way, you guys,

00:04:54.200 --> 00:04:57.033
congratulations.
"Cocaine Bear."

00:04:57.033 --> 00:04:58.634
Unbelievable.
-Amazing. Yeah.

00:04:58.634 --> 00:05:00.534
Yes.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:00.534 --> 00:05:02.367
-The two of you
collaborating again.

00:05:02.367 --> 00:05:04.467
And also with Margo Martindale
from "The Americans."

00:05:04.467 --> 00:05:06.901
-It was an "Americans" reunion.
We loved it.

00:05:06.901 --> 00:05:08.868
But congratulations,
Elizabeth Banks,

00:05:08.868 --> 00:05:10.901
who pulled that
incredible movie off.

00:05:10.901 --> 00:05:12.934
-It's a delight.
It's the kind of movie

00:05:12.934 --> 00:05:14.267
that people want to go see
in theaters again,

00:05:14.267 --> 00:05:15.901
and we just need
more and more of those.

00:05:15.901 --> 00:05:17.534
-I say yes.
-But "The Americans,"

00:05:17.534 --> 00:05:19.200
you were very honest,
which I appreciated,

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:20.801
that it was
a very complicated plot.

00:05:20.801 --> 00:05:22.501
And, you know,
there was a lot of subterfuge

00:05:22.501 --> 00:05:24.801
and a lot of people pretending.
And you just straight-up

00:05:24.801 --> 00:05:27.267
admitted to us
you could never follow it.

00:05:27.267 --> 00:05:30.434
-I had the entire production
team, the entire writing staff.

00:05:30.434 --> 00:05:32.100
I still was like, "I have
no idea what's going on."

00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:33.434
[ Laughter ]

00:05:33.434 --> 00:05:36.634
I freely admit I'm not
the sharpest tool in the box.

00:05:36.634 --> 00:05:39.834
I'm probably the biggest tool
in the wardrobe.

00:05:39.834 --> 00:05:41.467
But I'm like,
"This is so complicated.

00:05:41.467 --> 00:05:42.934
I have no idea what's going on."
-Look, some people

00:05:42.934 --> 00:05:44.834
can follow plots, and some
people are leek eaters.

00:05:44.834 --> 00:05:46.367
-I like to think
I'm the Everyman.

00:05:46.367 --> 00:05:49.434
I'm like, "Look, if
I understand it, we're golden."

00:05:49.434 --> 00:05:51.300
If not --"
And everyone will be going,

00:05:51.300 --> 00:05:53.033
"We all understand it
except you."

00:05:53.033 --> 00:05:55.367
And I'm like, "All right."

00:05:55.367 --> 00:05:57.200
I'm thinking for the other...
half?

00:05:57.200 --> 00:05:59.267
-Because "Perry Mason" --
now it's "Perry Mason."

00:05:59.267 --> 00:06:03.267
It's a courtroom drama.
It's, you know, legal maneuvers.

00:06:03.267 --> 00:06:04.400
Are you the same?

00:06:04.400 --> 00:06:05.767
-I had no idea
what was going on.

00:06:05.767 --> 00:06:07.634
-Yeah.
-I was forever going,

00:06:07.634 --> 00:06:09.767
"Who is he?"
[ Laughter ]

00:06:09.767 --> 00:06:11.534
He's like, "That's the guy
you're defending!"

00:06:11.534 --> 00:06:13.501
I was like, "What? I thought
I was defending the other guy."

00:06:13.501 --> 00:06:15.767
"That's his brother!"
I was like, "oh, my God."

00:06:15.767 --> 00:06:17.267
This is --
My head is spinning.

00:06:17.267 --> 00:06:18.834
-You're a fantastic actor

00:06:18.834 --> 00:06:20.634
because you come off
so sharp on camera.

00:06:20.634 --> 00:06:22.000
-That's where my acting --

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:23.634
that's where the acting
comes in.

00:06:23.634 --> 00:06:24.934
-Yeah.
Unbelievable.

00:06:24.934 --> 00:06:26.200
[ Applause ]
-Unbelievable.

00:06:26.200 --> 00:06:29.367
-Well, I really -- you know,
I know you're a busy man

00:06:29.367 --> 00:06:31.501
and, you know, scheduling
is always an issue.

00:06:31.501 --> 00:06:34.267
But, man, we should make
St. David's a tradition here.

00:06:34.267 --> 00:06:35.534
-Bring back day drinking.

00:06:35.534 --> 00:06:37.167
We'll do it on March the 1st.
-Oh, there you go.

00:06:37.167 --> 00:06:39.100
Day drinking with a Welsh theme.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:39.100 --> 00:06:41.467
Matthew Rhys!
Second season of "Perry Mason"

00:06:41.467 --> 00:06:43.934
premieres March 6th
on HBO and HBO Max.

00:06:43.934 --> 00:06:45.968
We'll be right back
with Francia Raisa.

